<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:blockml="org.blockml.bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:def="org.blockml.bml.definition"
  xmlns:cli="org.blockml.bml.cli"
  xmlns:cliapi="org.blockml.bml.cli.api"
  xmlns:clicap="org.blockml.bml.cli.capability"
  xmlns:clicommand="org.blockml.bml.cli.command"
  xmlns:cliconfig="org.blockml.bml.cli.config"
  xmlns:clidocumentation="org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation"
  xmlns:runtime="org.blockml.bml.compiler.runtime"
  xmlns:framework="org.blockml.bml.framework"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation">

  <name>LayerSeparation</name>
  <type>clidocumentation:LayerSeparation</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>CLI vs compiler vs framework vs targets</is>

  <documentation>Layers relevant to the CLI:

    org.blockml.bml.cli.* (this package) — commands, args, config, bootstrap order, file I/O.

    @blockml/compiler — compileToOutput, CompileRequest, Target Registry, compile scope resolution (C7).
    CLI builds requests; compiler owns facade semantics.

    @blockml/framework — bootstrapTypeRegistry, TypeRegistry. CLI wraps as bootstrapProjectTypeRegistry.

    @blockml/transformer — sequential workflow Stages on a ModelTransformation. CLI wraps as RunTransform and supplies default Execute and Reflect agents.

    @blockml/graph — authored structural graph. CLI wraps as RunGraph.

    @blockml/builder — BomBuilder session. CLI wraps as RunNew.

    Target packages (@blockml/blockdoc-target, xsd-target, fatblock-target) — RenderTarget impls
    and targetOptions types. CLI registers via bootstrapTargets; does not own render algorithms.

    @machineblocks/cli — domain host for SCAD product; out of scope for this library.</documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="clidocumentation:ArchitectureOverview" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>

</block>
